From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] win32: include dxgi1_2 and DXGI headers before d3d11_1.h

The Windows x64 llvm-mingw toolchain fails to compile
modules/video_output/win32/direct3d11.c because d3d11_1.h needs DXGI types to
be available first. The include-order fix solved DXGI_COLOR_SPACE_TYPE, but the
x64 contrib header set still leaves IDXGIResource1 and
DXGI_SHARED_RESOURCE_READ/WRITE undeclared unless dxgi1_2.h is brought in
explicitly before d3d11_1.h:

  unknown type name 'IDXGIResource1'

Include dxgi1_2.h explicitly and keep the DXGI headers before d3d11_1.h so the
needed DXGI declarations are available first without redefining the color-space
enum from dxgi1_4.
---
 modules/video_output/win32/direct3d11.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/video_output/win32/direct3d11.c b/modules/video_output/win32/direct3d11.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/modules/video_output/win32/direct3d11.c
+++ b/modules/video_output/win32/direct3d11.c
@@ -20,12 +20,13 @@
 
 #define COBJMACROS
 #include <initguid.h>
-#include <d3d11_1.h>
+#include <dxgi1_2.h>
 #ifdef HAVE_DXGI1_6_H
 # include <dxgi1_6.h>
 #else
 # include <dxgi1_5.h>
 #endif
+#include <d3d11_1.h>
 #ifdef HAVE_D3D11_4_H
 #include <d3d11_4.h>
 #endif